{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you had a rough day at dialysis. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. I went for my regular dialysis, but I started feeling weak. My blood pressure dropped and my heart slowed down. They said my potassium was very high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:36:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Your potassium was 8.6, which is dangerously high. That can cause your heart to slow down. You were given calcium, insulin, and other treatments in the ER to bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:37:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember getting a shot and feeling a bit better. But why did this happen? I’ve been careful with my diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:38:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not entirely sure, but one possibility is that you didn’t complete your last dialysis session. That can let potassium build up. You mentioned having some diarrhea today—did that affect your treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:40:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did have some loose stools after lunch. I didn’t think it was serious. I also may have missed a few pills, but I can’t remember which ones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-10-16 17:41:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could play a role. Diarrhea and missed medications, especially blood pressure drugs like lisinopril, can affect your potassium. We’ve started you on emergency dialysis to clear it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-10-16 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your dialysis went well. Your potassium is now down to a safer level. Your heart rate has improved too—from the 20s to the 50s. You no longer need the dopamine support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-10-16 18:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But I felt a little shaky after the insulin. Was that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-10-16 18:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the insulin helped lower your potassium but caused a brief drop in blood sugar. We gave you dextrose, and it corrected quickly. Your diabetes is stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-10-16 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your heart enzymes and ECG. No signs of a heart attack. The slow rhythm was likely due to the high potassium. Your heart should stay stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-10-16 19:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been through enough heart issues. What about my other medications? Should I keep taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-10-16 19:02:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held your lisinopril temporarily because it can raise potassium. Now that your levels are better, we’re restarting it—but at a lower dose, 20 mg daily instead of 40."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-10-16 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray showed some fluid around the lungs, but it hasn’t changed much. It’s likely related to your heart condition, not an infection. Your blood cultures came back negative, so we stopped antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-10-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well overnight. Your repeat labs show normal potassium and stable kidney function. The dialysis team will see you tomorrow as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-10-17 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-10-17 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you. Remember to complete all your dialysis sessions, watch your weight—call if you gain more than 3 pounds—and take your meds as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-10-17 08:04:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. I’ll be more careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-10-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—we’ve added a stool softener in case you have more diarrhea. It can affect your electrolytes. Keep us posted if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-10-17 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll watch for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-10-17 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your wife mentioned you felt some neck weakness earlier. Are you still having that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-10-17 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s better now. I think it was just from being weak at dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-10-17 12:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely due to the electrolyte imbalance. It should continue improving. Just keep up with your care and follow up with your nephrologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-10-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your discharge meds. Everything is the same except for the lower lisinopril dose and the addition of senna for constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-10-17 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to take them correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-10-17 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You can head home soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-10-17 15:31:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-10-17 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call your doctor if you feel dizzy, short of breath, or notice rapid weight gain. You’re scheduled for dialysis tomorrow—don’t miss it."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-10-16 17:34:00",
